# __APP_NAME__ (App Service Builder + AI Gateway)

__USER_INTENT__

A minimal Python chat agent built with [Microsoft Agent Framework](https://github.com/microsoft/agent-framework) and FastAPI, packaged for [Azure App Service Builder](https://aka.ms/embr) (`builder.yaml`) and connected to [Azure AI Gateway](https://ai.gateway.azure.com).

## Architecture

```text
Browser UI (/) ──► FastAPI + Agent Framework (/api/chat/stream) ──► Azure AI Gateway (/openai/v1) ──► Model
```

- `builder.yaml` declares the App Service Builder web service (`port: 8080`, `healthCheckPath: /health`).
- `app.py` serves the chat UI (`/`) and SSE streaming endpoint (`POST /api/chat/stream`).
- `config.py` and `gateway.py` configure `OpenAIChatCompletionClient` against Azure AI Gateway using either your local `.env` (`AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL`, `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`, `AI_GATEWAY_MODEL`) or Azure Managed Identity (`AZURE_AI_GATEWAY_HOST`, `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`).

## Local Setup & Run

1. Connect an Azure AI Gateway and model in the **Connect** step (which writes `.env` / `src/agent/.env`), or configure `.env` manually:
   ```bash
   AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://<gateway>.gateway.ai.azure.com/openai/v1
   AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=<key>
   AI_GATEWAY_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
   ```
2. Start the app:
   - macOS / Linux:
     ```bash
     ./scripts/dev-start.sh
     ```
   - Windows PowerShell:
     ```powershell
     .\scripts\dev-start.ps1
     ```
3. Open `http://127.0.0.1:8080` in your browser or use the **Open web app** button in Run mode.

## Run Tests

